## Data Optimization Rules

### 1. Document Size Limits
- Maximum 1MB per document
- Activity documents: ~2-5KB targeted
- Insight documents: ~10-50KB targeted
- User documents: ~5-10KB targeted

### 2. Collection Organization
- Group related data using subcollections
- Keep frequently accessed data at the top level
- Archive old data to archival collections

### 3. Query Optimization
```typescript
// Good: Use indexed fields
const activities = await db
  .collection('users')
  .doc(userId)
  .collection('activities')
  .where('timestamp', '>=', startTime)
  .where('timestamp', '<=', endTime)
  .orderBy('timestamp', 'desc')
  .limit(100)
  .get();

// Bad: Fetch too much data
const allActivities = await db
  .collection('users')
  .doc(userId)
  .collection('activities')
  .get(); // Fetches all data

// Good: Use pagination
const firstPage = await db
  .collection('users')
  .doc(userId)
  .collection('activities')
  .orderBy('timestamp', 'desc')
  .limit(25)
  .get();

const lastDoc = firstPage.docs[firstPage.docs.length - 1];
const nextPage = await db
  .collection('users')
  .doc(userId)
  .collection('activities')
  .orderBy('timestamp', 'desc')
  .startAfter(lastDoc)
  .limit(25)
  .get();
```

### 4. Data Cleanup Strategy
- Daily activities: Archive after 90 days
- Temporary insights: Delete after 30 days
- Error logs: Delete after 7 days
- Performance metrics: Aggregate and delete after 30 days

### 5. Real-time vs Batch Processing
- Real-time: Critical notifications, instant feedback
- Batch: Daily/weekly reports, statistics calculations
- Scheduled: Data cleanup, analytics calculations

